# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Tooling caches
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Coverage reports — never commit; regenerated by `uv run pytest`
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Runtime state (externalize to a volume / backing service — never commit)
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*-wal
*-shm
*.log
*.gz

# Local env / secrets
.env
.env.*

# furnace local state — regenerated on each deploy / stoke, never authored.
# `.furnace/pin.toml` is NOT here: the template pin is real config and stays tracked.
.furnace/deployed.json
.furnace/spans.json

# Laid by gavel, regenerable by the next order — never this repo's source. These
# three used to reach a newborn through `furnace ignite`, which appended them at
# birth (`ensure_gitignore`); the applier lays and appends nothing, so the
# template says it instead. The base store keeps one blob per laid file so the
# next order can tell a hub move from a local edit. `.claude/` too: the note
# beside .specify/ below calls it "same category" and the three sibling
# templates list it, but this file never did — `ignite` was writing it.
.claude/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.furnace/base/

# Agent worktrees — ephemeral isolation scratch from Agent(isolation: worktree)
.claude/worktrees/

# spec-kit's surface, laid down by `specify init` as a copier task and
# regenerable by it. Same category as .claude/ — poured by a tool, not
# authored here.
# It was tracked anyway in 42 repos (1,005 files, ~24 per repo), which is not
# a decision anybody wrote down: only .specify/feature.json was ever ignored.
.specify/

# Agent session locks. .claude/hooks/agent_lock.py writes .agent-locks/<session>.json
# at SessionStart and unlinks it at SessionEnd; a dead pid's lock is reaped on the
# next read. Per-machine runtime state keyed to a live pid — worthless to any other
# clone, meaningless once the process exits. The machine-global excludes file carries
# this for clones that already exist; the template is what makes a struck star carry
# it on its own.
.agent-locks/
# <<< python-repo-template <<<
